refer 00w1.c and 00w2.c

	• Both programs write to the same file concurrently
	• Each write is only one byte long
	• No synchronization (locks, semaphores) is used
	• This results in a race condition
	• Output in the file is interleaved and non-deterministic


critical section of code 
------------------------

	The part of the program where we trying to access shared resource is crtical section of the code 

	A shared resource must be accessed by only one process at a time 

	Before entering the critical section, a process must check whether the shared resource is free
	
	If the resource is free : 

		The process locks the resource 
		Enters the critical section 

	While one process is inside the critical section : 

		Other processes must wait 

	After completing the operation : 

		The process unlocks the resource 
		Other processes can then enter the critical section 
